@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Retained restore procedure — private operator/legacy workflow only
start
:Operator uses an explicit private recovery context;\npublic /api/workspace/backups routes are unavailable;
:Validate ZIP paths, size, checksums,\nworkspace document and referenced audio;
if (Archive valid?) then (yes)
  :Authorize import scope;\ncreate an expiring preview with counts\nand captured workspace version;
else (no)
  :Reject; leave live logical data unchanged;
  stop
endif
if (Confirmed REPLACE?) then (yes)
  :Acquire shared/private workspace lock;
else (no)
  :Leave live data unchanged; preview expires;
  stop
endif
if (Preview valid and version unchanged?) then (yes)
  :Revalidate archive and authorization;\ncreate verified pre-restore safety backup;
else (no)
  :Reject stale/expired/unauthorized preview;\nrelease lock;
  stop
endif
if (Safety copy and media staging succeed?) then (yes)
  :Apply validated logical data in a\nversion-checked SQLite transaction;
else (no)
  :Clean up newly staged files;\nrelease lock; report failure;
  stop
endif
if (Transaction commits?) then (yes)
  :Invalidate preview and remove used preview ZIP;
  if (Post-commit cleanup succeeds?) then (yes)
    :Report counts and safety backup ID;
  else (no)
    :Report uncertain completion;\ninspect saved state before retrying;
  endif
else (no)
  :Roll back logical rows;\nremove newly staged files; report error;
endif
:Release lock; retain safety backup\nand earlier committed media for recovery;
stop
legend bottom
  Shared format 5 includes ownership, request mappings, archived profiles and readings; format 4 remains compatible.
  Private formats 1/2 normalize to format 3; outer ZIP manifest is format 1.
  Non-system legacy restore cannot change another creator's records or original archived profiles.
  PublicWorkspaceStore.authorize_import() always rejects; no browser restore feature is implied.
  Filesystem staging and SQLite are coordinated operations, not one cross-file ACID transaction.
endlegend
@enduml
